  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Keerthikumar vs The Commissioner on 22 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 22.11.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P (MD).No.27259 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)Nos.23070, 23072 & 23074 of 2024 Keerthikumar ...Petitioner Vs. 1.The Commissioner, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Dms Campus, 5th Floor, No.359, Annasalai, Teynampet, Chennai-6. 2.The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Viswanathapuram, Madurai, Madurai District. 3.The Food Safety Officer, Madurai Corporation (Code No.573) Madurai. ...Responde Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution o issue a Writ of Certiorari, to call for the records relating to the impu proceedings bearing Na.Ka.No.2223/A2/2024/U.Pa.Thu passed by the second respondent, dated 03.10.2024 and quash the same. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/6 W.P ( Keerthikumar vs The Commissioner on 22 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/149924696/ 1 For Petitioner : Mr.M.Gnana Gurunathan For R1 & R2 : Mr.M.Senthil Ayyanar Government Advocate For R3 : Mrs.S.Devasena Standing Counsel ORDER",
    "facts": "He is selling only the STASH Pro Rolling Paper for the purpose of packaging the food. Except this material, no other food products or Tobacco are selling in the petty shop. Therefore, the respondents have no jurisdiction to lock and seal the premises. That apart, the lock and seal was ordered without even mentioning the period. After registration of FIR, no complaint has been filed by the respondents before the Adjudicating authority to prosecute the petitioner. The petitioner claims to be a owner of the premises and filed this writ petition.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
